<title>JAPAN: Nissho Iwai buys Coors can recycling plant.</title>
<headline>Nissho Iwai buys Coors can recycling plant.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissho Iwai Corp said on Tuesday it bought an aluminium can recycling center in California from an affiliate of U.S. brewer Adolph Coors Co.</p>
<p>The facility recovers and processes 800 to 1,000 tonnes of used beverage cans per month. It also process used PET bottles, glass and paper, the company said.</p>
<p>Nissho Iwai and two of its U.S. subsidiaries established a new company, Nac Recycling Inc, capitalised at $500,000, to operate the facility and market its output.</p>
<p>Nissho Iwai said Nac Recycling's output would be refined in the U.S. on a tolling basis and exported to Japan or sold directly to U.S. processors.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
